      "id": "table-3",
      "line": 314,
      "heading_context": "## Decision Cheat Sheet",
      "headers": [
        "Question",
        "Answer"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Which texture holds the most plant-available water?",
          "Silt loam — large surface area without too-tight micropores; holds maximum capillary water"
        ],
        [
          "Which texture drains fastest?",
          "Sandy; macropores dominate; water moves by gravity rapidly"
        ],
        [
          "What creates granular structure?",
          "Biological activity: earthworms, fungal hyphae (glomalin), organic matter; aggregation by root exudates"
        ],
        [
          "What destroys granular structure fastest?",
          "Tillage; also sodium (Na+) dispersion in sodic soils; raindrop impact on bare surface"
        ],
        [
          "What is bulk density and why does it matter?",
          "Mass/volume ratio including pores; > 1.6 g/cm³ in loam = compaction restricting root growth"
        ],
        [
          "What does a platy structure indicate?",
          "Compaction (surface traffic, tillage compaction below plow depth); poor aeration and drainage"
        ],
        [
          "How do you determine texture in the field without a lab?",
          "Ribbon test: feel for grittiness (sand), silkiness (silt), plasticity and stickiness (clay)"
        ]
      ]
    }
  ]
